WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.400 --> 00:06.401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:06.411 --> 00:08.400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

4
00:08.430 --> 00:09.950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

5
00:10.000 --> 00:11.501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

6
00:11.511 --> 00:12.890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

7
00:12.899 --> 00:13.900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

8
00:13.911 --> 00:14.912
[or any particular group of people.]

9
00:14.926 --> 00:16.640
But I really don't want to go home.

10
00:16.707 --> 00:19.720
Why don't you stay here with me for one night?

11
00:19.880 --> 00:21.440
I'll let you go wherever you want.

12
00:21.481 --> 00:23.000
Except to see that woman.

13
00:23.082 --> 00:24.720
Throw that away. I'll buy you a new one.

14
00:24.800 --> 00:26.960
You're so mean! I hate you when you're like this!

15
00:27.054 --> 00:30.920
- Who taught you to talk like that? - You wicked mother!

16
00:31.787 --> 00:32.788
Titus! Titus!

17
00:33.339 --> 00:36.720
This is what I'll use to prove that Nopnapha ordered my sister's murder.

18
00:36.747 --> 00:38.840
I've already gotten close to her younger child.

19
00:38.912 --> 00:40.974
Now I'll find a way to get close to the older one.

20
00:41.064 --> 00:42.480
I'm sure I'll uncover plenty more useful information.

21
00:42.547 --> 00:45.600
Munin, I signed the Smart Card project contract today.

22
00:45.630 --> 00:49.000
But weren't you planning to sabotage the project to ruin Nopnapha's reputation?

23
00:49.031 --> 00:51.320
If she goes down, we go down with her.

24
00:51.366 --> 00:54.200
I promise I won't put our company at risk.

25
00:54.267 --> 00:57.120
Get this phone checked for Nopnapha's fingerprints.

26
00:57.611 --> 00:59.240
The fingerprint results are back.

27
00:59.376 --> 01:01.520
There's no trace of Nopnapha's fingerprints!

28
01:01.678 --> 01:02.880
Then whose fingerprints are on it?

29
01:03.016 --> 01:05.560
Jenphop's. His are the only fingerprints on it.

30
01:05.859 --> 01:09.060
The phone belongs to Jenphop, not Nopnapha.

31
01:09.800 --> 01:10.801
Munin!

32
01:10.990 --> 01:14.120
You've been going after the wrong person all along!

33
01:17.238 --> 01:19.040
Is the fried chicken good, sweetie?

34
01:19.110 --> 01:22.320
It's delicious, Mom! Can you make it for me every day?

35
01:22.451 --> 01:23.600
Of course, sweetheart.

36
01:23.891 --> 01:27.491
Hurry up and finish eating. Daddy will take you to the mall afterward.

37
01:27.518 --> 01:30.280
Yay! I love Mom and Dad more than anything.

38
01:34.192 --> 01:36.193
You kids are always playing make-believe.

39
01:37.974 --> 01:40.320
Families like that don't exist in real life.

40
01:40.560 --> 01:43.760
If they did, would you two be sitting here playing with trash?

41
01:45.878 --> 01:49.320
You crazy old hag! Just because you can't find a husband doesn't mean you have to run your mouth!

42
01:49.611 --> 01:51.880
You little brat, Nin! Watch your filthy mouth!

43
01:54.342 --> 01:56.000
Why the hell did you slap me?

44
01:56.118 --> 01:57.119
You crazy little bitch!

45
02:03.048 --> 02:05.360
You're no match for me, you little orphan brat!

46
02:06.350 --> 02:07.440
Even your parents don't love you!

47
02:08.035 --> 02:12.000
You'll never have the happy family you've always dreamed of!

48
02:12.318 --> 02:13.319
Mark my words!

49
02:23.319 --> 02:25.280
Ta, don't listen to her.

50
02:25.424 --> 02:28.600
When we grow up, we'll get married and have kids.

51
02:28.760 --> 02:31.246
And we'll build happy, loving families, Ta.

52
02:31.550 --> 02:34.051
We'll build houses right next to each other.

53
02:34.190 --> 02:36.760
And our kids can play together too.

54
02:36.779 --> 02:37.780
Yeah.

55
04:01.480 --> 04:04.712
Do you really think these two things are connected?

56
04:08.566 --> 04:09.567
It's possible.

57
04:11.046 --> 04:14.123
My sister got pregnant, and the Director told her to have an abortion.

58
04:14.860 --> 04:15.861
Ta refused.

59
04:16.875 --> 04:17.876
So he ordered her killed.

60
04:19.739 --> 04:21.720
When you first went back to see the Director,

61
04:22.326 --> 04:25.170
did he seem shocked or surprised at all?

62
04:32.672 --> 04:33.673
Oh.

63
04:34.491 --> 04:35.600
You're back at work?

64
04:36.235 --> 04:37.600
Yes, Director.

65
04:40.683 --> 04:42.619
He didn't seem particularly surprised.

66
04:43.787 --> 04:46.080
When I talked to him alone in his office,

67
04:46.683 --> 04:48.920
he didn't show any signs of having ordered Ta's murder.

68
04:51.886 --> 04:53.520
Or maybe he's just really good at hiding it.

69
04:53.966 --> 04:55.520
When he found out the killer had failed,

70
04:55.608 --> 04:57.640
he might've pretended nothing had happened.

71
05:01.360 --> 05:03.000
But he did ask about the pregnancy.

72
05:04.000 --> 05:06.040
He even seemed concerned about Ta's miscarriage.

73
05:08.544 --> 05:11.680
Didn't your sister mention her pregnancy or miscarriage in her diary?

74
05:17.542 --> 05:20.520
If she didn't write everything down,

75
05:21.670 --> 05:25.840
there could be a lot more about her that we don't know.

76
05:27.950 --> 05:29.080
Are you saying

77
05:30.648 --> 05:32.240
my sister might've had trouble with someone else,

78
05:32.520 --> 05:35.400
besides Nopnapha and Jenphop?

79
05:37.870 --> 05:40.376
Yeah, it's possible.

80
05:43.304 --> 05:45.200
I'm just saying we should consider every possibility.

81
05:46.464 --> 05:49.019
Her diary doesn't tell us everything about her life.

82
05:53.211 --> 05:55.046
Looks like we'll have to dig even deeper from now on

83
05:55.952 --> 05:57.300
and stop jumping to conclusions.

84
05:59.334 --> 06:01.100
I don't want to take revenge on the wrong person.

85
06:06.123 --> 06:07.867
But based on the clues we have so far,

86
06:10.059 --> 06:11.520
our prime suspect

87
06:12.566 --> 06:13.640
is Jenphop.

88
06:25.567 --> 06:26.568
Stop.

89
06:28.104 --> 06:29.120
The Minister wants to see you.

90
06:30.366 --> 06:32.967
Apparently, she wants to thank you for looking after Titus last night.

91
06:33.500 --> 06:34.501
No thanks necessary.

92
06:34.700 --> 06:36.960
Just consider it an act of charity for a lousy mother.

93
06:37.283 --> 06:38.560
- I'm not going. - Hey!

94
06:39.486 --> 06:41.614
Who the hell do you think you are?

95
06:42.323 --> 06:44.250
Don't get too full of yourself. Come with me.

96
06:44.600 --> 06:47.320
You're just a lackey. No need to act so tough.

97
06:48.144 --> 06:50.920
Go tell your boss I'm not coming.

98
06:51.838 --> 06:53.600
Are you coming willingly, or do I have to drag you by the hair?

99
06:53.639 --> 06:55.960
I'm not scared of you. I've got fists and feet too, you know.

100
06:56.240 --> 06:57.241
You bitch, Mutta!

101
07:01.046 --> 07:03.056
What do you want, Nopnapha?

102
07:08.123 --> 07:10.920
Stop Director Jenphop and Veekit right now.

103
07:10.987 --> 07:12.560
Yes, of course.

104
07:14.240 --> 07:17.760
Chuenchom, Mrs. Nopnapha's about to slap Mutta again.

105
07:18.536 --> 07:20.180
We have to keep Veekit away.

106
07:26.232 --> 07:27.960
Pee standing up like a real man.

107
07:29.539 --> 07:31.240
Want to pee together, Veekit?

108
07:33.043 --> 07:34.160
I'm here to take a dump.

109
07:41.966 --> 07:44.131
Being a man must be so convenient.

110
07:44.376 --> 07:46.130
Just give it a little shake, and you're all clean.

111
08:05.500 --> 08:06.501
Hey!

112
08:06.800 --> 08:08.001
- What's that? - What's that?

113
08:08.872 --> 08:09.873
What's going on?

114
08:12.500 --> 08:13.501
Hey!

115
08:16.158 --> 08:17.250
Get your camera ready, you old hag!

116
08:27.587 --> 08:29.500
- Hello, sir. - Hey! Why are you blocking the way?

117
08:29.811 --> 08:31.012
Do you know who I am?

118
08:31.411 --> 08:34.328
There's an eight-meter-deep sinkhole up ahead, sir.

119
08:34.680 --> 08:36.558
If you fall in, you're as good as dead.

120
08:37.208 --> 08:38.209
Please go this way instead.

121
08:40.147 --> 08:41.148
Let's go that way. Come on.

122
08:45.496 --> 08:48.160
We really have a knack for sticking our noses into things.

123
08:48.486 --> 08:51.900
We always show up just in time for a historic moment.

124
08:51.920 --> 08:52.921
Yeah.

125
08:53.200 --> 08:54.400
No filming, please.

126
08:54.659 --> 08:59.741
Today, Mrs. Nopnapha is about to slap that shameless bitch Mutta again!

127
09:00.094 --> 09:01.095
Go ahead, ma'am.

128
09:02.510 --> 09:04.101
It's been months since you last got slapped.

129
09:04.814 --> 09:06.415
You must miss the sting of my hand.

130
09:07.310 --> 09:08.520
I'll give you another taste.

131
09:09.376 --> 09:12.240
Consider it my way of thanking you for taking such good care of my daughter.

132
09:17.631 --> 09:18.622
You bitch!

133
09:18.628 --> 09:20.480
What an idiot! Go grab her by the hair!

134
09:20.996 --> 09:21.997
Get over here!

135
09:43.043 --> 09:45.640
Grandpa's hair, Grandma's hair, everyone's hair!

136
09:46.379 --> 09:48.380
Do you even have any real hair, Mutta?

137
09:48.651 --> 09:50.252
I bet your whole head is fake, you bitch!

138
09:50.300 --> 09:52.200
You'd even let yourself get hurt to please your boss.

139
09:52.806 --> 09:54.520
I hope she gives you a raise.

140
09:54.807 --> 09:55.808
You filthy lowlife!

141
09:56.872 --> 09:58.073
A legendary slap like this?

142
09:59.214 --> 10:00.920
I've got to see it up close!

143
10:02.190 --> 10:03.680
- Hurry up! - I'm coming!

144
10:06.700 --> 10:07.701
You bitch, Mutta!

145
10:07.768 --> 10:10.040
You keep calling my name! What, is it your mother's name too?

146
10:11.550 --> 10:12.551
Ouch! That was savage!

147
10:17.150 --> 10:18.151
Who locked the door?

148
10:19.496 --> 10:21.920
Is anyone out there? Can someone open the door?

149
10:23.541 --> 10:24.600
Hello? Is anyone out there?

150
10:25.723 --> 10:28.240
- Please open the door! - Hurry! Mrs. Nopnapha's about to slap that homewrecking bitch again!

151
10:28.250 --> 10:29.920
Seriously? Let's go!

152
10:30.251 --> 10:31.252
Ta!

153
10:31.739 --> 10:33.640
Help! Someone open the door!

154
10:34.214 --> 10:35.766
Shit! What the hell?

155
10:40.827 --> 10:41.828
That's what happens when you get old.

156
10:42.923 --> 10:43.960
You've got quite a mouth on you, bitch!

157
10:57.838 --> 10:59.280
Everyone, take a good look at this woman!

158
10:59.840 --> 11:03.080
She thinks she can abuse anyone just because she's powerful.

159
11:03.606 --> 11:06.440
Today, someone who was once her victim is fighting back!

160
11:06.683 --> 11:07.684
Open the damn door!

161
11:10.360 --> 11:11.361
Ta!

162
11:11.440 --> 11:13.280
I won't let history repeat itself.

163
11:13.851 --> 11:15.280
These steps outside the Ministry

164
11:15.872 --> 11:17.873
are going to taste your filthy blood for a change.

165
11:34.000 --> 11:35.001
Everyone.

166
11:35.027 --> 11:37.240
Mrs. Nopnapha's coming! Move!

167
11:45.894 --> 11:46.895
Is she going to die?

168
11:46.966 --> 11:50.000
Mutta! You slapped me!

169
11:50.320 --> 11:51.921
You're going to die a horrible death!

170
11:52.630 --> 11:55.080
No, you're the one who's going to die a horrible death.

171
12:24.470 --> 12:25.840
Let me wash your face for you.

172
12:27.760 --> 12:29.461
So you can pass on to a better afterlife.

173
12:33.366 --> 12:34.440
Congratulations!

174
12:34.795 --> 12:38.196
The legendary slap outside the Ministry will go down in history

175
12:38.800 --> 12:39.960
with your name instead of Mutta's.

176
12:48.060 --> 12:49.061
Give it back!

177
12:52.462 --> 12:53.463
What?

178
12:53.648 --> 12:54.680
My hairpiece!

179
12:55.398 --> 12:56.699
Look at all these split ends!

180
12:57.718 --> 13:00.040
You really should get a hair treatment. Here!

181
13:07.960 --> 13:10.660
Napha, why are you lying on the ground?

182
13:13.214 --> 13:15.963
That bitch Mutta slapped me down the stairs.

183
13:16.662 --> 13:18.680
Come help me up. I'm in so much pain.

184
13:19.552 --> 13:20.553
Whoa!

185
13:20.710 --> 13:22.711
I can't. I've got a bad back.

186
13:23.062 --> 13:25.728
Hey, Thaithat! Call an ambulance!

187
13:25.995 --> 13:27.560
Tell them it's urgent! It's an emergency.

188
13:31.900 --> 13:32.901
Hey!

189
13:33.400 --> 13:34.774
What are you all staring at?

190
13:35.100 --> 13:36.400
Come on, move along!

191
13:37.446 --> 13:39.480
The show's over. Get back to work!

192
13:39.664 --> 13:41.165
It was just getting good.

193
13:43.721 --> 13:45.480
That was brutal, I'm telling you.

194
13:47.800 --> 13:48.801
Uncle Phop.

195
13:50.584 --> 13:52.560
Do you really think someone can change that much?

196
13:54.406 --> 13:56.520
Ta's like a completely different person now.

197
13:59.432 --> 14:01.880
Hey, isn't that a good thing?

198
14:03.374 --> 14:05.400
Now Napha won't dare mess with her again.

199
14:11.398 --> 14:12.399
Yes, please.

200
14:13.366 --> 14:15.567
I'd like some bright, colorful flowers.

201
14:17.472 --> 14:18.473
Thank you.

202
14:23.915 --> 14:26.416
Hong, where is everyone?

203
14:28.248 --> 14:30.280
They're downstairs gossiping.

204
14:31.672 --> 14:34.142
Want to know what they're saying, Ta?

205
14:34.482 --> 14:35.483
No.

206
14:39.168 --> 14:40.600
They're saying

207
14:41.584 --> 14:44.600
being the Director's mistress is bad enough,

208
14:45.312 --> 14:47.640
but slapping his wife down the stairs

209
14:48.272 --> 14:50.683
makes you a hundred times worse.

210
14:51.936 --> 14:55.720
Your name should go down in Thailand's history books

211
14:56.000 --> 14:59.520
as the most vicious mistress of all time.

212
15:00.539 --> 15:01.560
Who said that?

213
15:03.094 --> 15:04.640
I don't really know.

214
15:05.136 --> 15:08.440
I just overheard bits and pieces. I wasn't really listening.

215
15:10.936 --> 15:13.120
But everyone seems to agree

216
15:13.443 --> 15:15.121
that they're on the wife's side.

217
15:15.880 --> 15:17.920
Nobody's siding with the mistress.

218
15:18.881 --> 15:21.000
And whose side are you on, Hong?

219
15:25.627 --> 15:27.240
The mistress's side, of course.

220
15:28.422 --> 15:32.360
Because I'm on your side, Ta.

221
15:33.072 --> 15:34.073
You got this.

222
15:57.600 --> 15:58.501
[You bitch!]

223
15:58.600 --> 16:01.880
Nopnapha's and Oshi's X-ray results are both normal.

224
16:02.115 --> 16:04.160
But you may have some minor sprains.

225
16:04.170 --> 16:05.731
So I've put you in soft casts for now.

226
16:05.976 --> 16:08.500
You can take them off once you're feeling better.

227
16:09.550 --> 16:11.250
- Thank you, Doctor. - Thank you.

228
16:11.416 --> 16:12.417
Excuse me.

229
16:14.568 --> 16:16.800
I'm sorry I didn't get back in time to help you, ma'am.

230
16:17.952 --> 16:19.739
Oshi, what were you doing?

231
16:20.438 --> 16:21.648
I was helping her.

232
16:22.182 --> 16:23.800
She told me to strike first.

233
16:24.019 --> 16:25.020
And look what happened.

234
16:25.446 --> 16:28.047
I struck first, and now we're both swollen.

235
16:29.456 --> 16:31.232
You've made sure to keep this out of the news, right?

236
16:31.691 --> 16:33.520
I've already secured the CCTV footage.

237
16:35.947 --> 16:38.700
Hello, I've got a delivery.

238
16:38.747 --> 16:40.840
- Could you sign for it, please? - Sure.

239
16:44.624 --> 16:45.880
- Thank you. - Thank you.

240
16:54.211 --> 16:55.480
How thoughtful!

241
16:55.838 --> 16:58.270
Sending an electric fan instead of flowers to someone in the hospital.

242
16:58.872 --> 17:01.120
At least it's useful. I'll turn it on.

243
17:07.561 --> 17:09.480
Such a cool breeze.

244
17:09.782 --> 17:11.880
And it smells so fresh.

245
17:12.027 --> 17:14.328
Even though the flowers are fake.

246
17:17.467 --> 17:20.368
Sorry, there's something else. I forgot to attach it.

247
17:23.147 --> 17:24.648
There you go. Thank you.

248
17:27.238 --> 17:30.039
"With love and wicked wishes,

249
17:30.995 --> 17:32.480
Hope you die soon.

250
17:33.755 --> 17:34.756
From Mutta."

251
17:38.742 --> 17:41.734
Oshi, get a hitman to shoot that bitch right now!

252
17:42.600 --> 17:43.624
We can't do that, ma'am.

253
17:43.928 --> 17:45.680
We can't take risks like that anymore.

254
17:46.083 --> 17:47.864
If word gets out, it won't be worth it.

255
17:48.782 --> 17:52.174
Will you stop telling me what I can and can't do?

256
17:53.440 --> 17:56.350
It's your job to make sure nothing gets out.

257
17:57.432 --> 17:59.800
She's stealing my husband and my children!

258
17:59.859 --> 18:01.280
She slapped me down the stairs!

259
18:01.358 --> 18:04.600
And now she's sent me a funeral wreath fan to humiliate me!

260
18:05.192 --> 18:08.193
If I let her get away with this, don't call me Nopnapha.

261
18:10.520 --> 18:12.480
I'm not saying you shouldn't deal with her, ma'am.

262
18:12.931 --> 18:14.560
I'm just suggesting we find a way to do it through proper channels,

263
18:15.134 --> 18:16.960
so you won't have to put yourself at risk.

264
18:27.560 --> 18:29.107
You had to cause trouble again this morning?

265
18:30.392 --> 18:32.147
Nopnapha was the one who picked a fight with me.

266
18:32.159 --> 18:34.660
But you slapped her so hard she went tumbling down the stairs.

267
18:35.787 --> 18:38.059
And what about what happened at my house?

268
18:39.360 --> 18:41.561
You were the one who barged into my home.

269
18:41.627 --> 18:43.000
You started it, Ta.

270
18:43.488 --> 18:45.050
And do you know what's happened now?

271
18:45.459 --> 18:47.438
My daughter is insulting her own mother.

272
18:49.347 --> 18:51.048
That's because she treats her daughter badly.

273
18:51.614 --> 18:53.260
How is that my fault?

274
18:53.280 --> 18:54.940
Maybe not directly, but indirectly, Ta.

275
18:55.651 --> 18:58.280
If you hadn't gotten involved with Titus, none of this would've happened.

276
18:59.550 --> 19:00.551
Listen.

277
19:02.760 --> 19:04.040
I'm warning you.

278
19:05.190 --> 19:06.600
Stay away from Titus.

279
19:08.278 --> 19:10.279
And don't you ever set foot in my house again.

280
19:13.339 --> 19:16.160
Just because I love you doesn't mean I'll let you get away with everything, Ta.

281
19:17.424 --> 19:19.160
If you don't listen to me,

282
19:22.358 --> 19:24.560
I'll show you a side of me you've never seen before.

283
19:53.500 --> 19:54.901
Is that offer to take me out for dim sum still open?

284
19:55.800 --> 19:57.730
I've figured out why I never liked dim sum.

285
20:34.552 --> 20:36.803
I just haven't found a good place yet.

286
20:37.064 --> 20:38.880
Do you really like it?

287
20:40.424 --> 20:41.450
You're not just forcing yourself, are you?

288
20:44.158 --> 20:45.159
You're not just forcing yourself, are you?

289
20:47.928 --> 20:50.120
If you don't like it, you don't have to pretend.

290
20:50.558 --> 20:51.559
When you're with me,

291
20:52.862 --> 20:56.080
you don't have to be anyone else. Just be yourself, one hundred percent.

292
20:57.731 --> 20:59.170
I am being one hundred percent myself.

293
20:59.630 --> 21:00.631
I'm Mutta.

294
21:05.160 --> 21:07.161
But the Mutta I knew wasn't like this.

295
21:09.300 --> 21:11.920
Every day, we die and are reborn in a way.

296
21:12.601 --> 21:15.602
The Mutta you used to know is dead.

297
21:16.131 --> 21:18.960
The person sitting next to you now is someone else.

298
21:19.958 --> 21:21.559
Please accept the new me, Veekit.

299
21:25.142 --> 21:26.950
I'll try to understand what you're saying.

300
21:33.611 --> 21:34.612
It's Uncle Phop calling.

301
21:37.900 --> 21:38.901
Hello?

302
21:40.854 --> 21:43.855
Oh, I've already called the staff. They should be there this afternoon.

303
21:48.027 --> 21:50.028
I'll head over as soon as I finish eating.

304
21:52.955 --> 21:54.800
He scraped his car against a pole.

305
21:55.320 --> 21:56.520
So I had to call the insurance company for him.

306
21:59.267 --> 22:02.560
Does he make you handle everything whenever he has a problem?

307
22:04.627 --> 22:07.080
Yeah. I'm technically his secretary,

308
22:08.062 --> 22:09.200
but I'm also his nephew.

309
22:10.300 --> 22:12.601
So he keeps finding excuses to make me do things for him.

310
22:13.720 --> 22:16.880
Including illegal things?

311
22:17.494 --> 22:18.495
What do you mean?

312
22:19.200 --> 22:20.201
What are you getting at?

313
22:22.214 --> 22:25.800
Veekit, if you're sincere with me, tell me the truth.

314
22:28.032 --> 22:29.733
Has he ever made you do anything shady?

315
22:30.700 --> 22:32.320
What kind of shady things?

316
22:33.500 --> 22:34.560
What are you trying to say, Ta?

317
22:35.115 --> 22:36.400
Just tell me straight.

318
22:39.100 --> 22:42.001
Has he ever tried to hurt or kill anyone?

319
22:42.224 --> 22:43.225
Hey!

320
22:45.174 --> 22:46.340
Why are you asking me that?

321
22:48.966 --> 22:49.967
Just answer me, Veekit.

322
22:50.500 --> 22:51.501
Never.

323
22:52.920 --> 22:54.540
He's never asked me to do anything like that.

324
22:54.984 --> 22:56.485
And even if he did, I wouldn't do it.

325
22:57.838 --> 22:59.845
As for whether he's done anything himself, I don't know.

326
23:01.798 --> 23:03.440
Now it's your turn.

327
23:04.326 --> 23:05.627
Tell me what's going on.

328
23:08.475 --> 23:11.315
Nothing. I was just curious.

329
23:11.651 --> 23:14.080
I'm just worried that if I ever upset him,

330
23:14.398 --> 23:16.081
he might send someone to hurt me.

331
23:26.027 --> 23:29.690
According to our survey, our ministry is overstaffed.

332
23:30.832 --> 23:34.133
Some departments have dozens of employees, but only five actually work.

333
23:35.059 --> 23:37.460
The rest just sit around waiting for lunch every day.

334
23:37.918 --> 23:39.520
I've already spoken to the Civil Service Commission

335
23:39.880 --> 23:43.440
about cutting unnecessary positions.

336
23:53.700 --> 23:55.512
No way! I'm not resigning, no matter what!

337
23:55.608 --> 23:58.240
I've worked here for 20 years. That department head position should be mine!

338
23:58.309 --> 23:59.310
I'm not leaving!

339
23:59.646 --> 24:01.600
I'm not leaving either, Toey!

340
24:01.912 --> 24:03.200
Oh, come on! I've been working here...

341
24:03.240 --> 24:06.000
What about all those files, documents, and papers? They're so heavy! Who's going to carry them?

342
24:06.067 --> 24:08.000
These people can't even lift them.

343
24:08.220 --> 24:10.936
I paid 300,000 baht just to pass the civil service exam.

344
24:10.974 --> 24:13.819
I haven't even earned that money back yet. I'm not leaving.

345
24:13.862 --> 24:15.400
I'm not leaving either, Toey.

346
24:15.446 --> 24:18.440
If you fire me, I'll come scream in the cafeteria every day

347
24:18.457 --> 24:20.520
until you give me my job back.

348
24:20.822 --> 24:24.000
As for me, I'm smart, handsome,

349
24:24.163 --> 24:25.440
and talented.

350
24:25.886 --> 24:27.840
And most importantly, I'm a straight man.

351
24:28.000 --> 24:31.201
All I know how to do is make photocopies.

352
24:31.500 --> 24:34.601
If you fire me, how am I supposed to make a living?

353
24:34.601 --> 24:37.280
Then fire her. All she does is make photocopies anyway.

354
24:40.147 --> 24:41.480
Oh, stop it!

355
24:42.835 --> 24:44.200
Can you all stop panicking?

356
24:45.715 --> 24:48.080
They're not firing everyone, just two people.

357
24:54.278 --> 24:55.400
Hey, quiet!

358
24:59.190 --> 25:00.720
As for who's going to be let go,

359
25:00.843 --> 25:02.800
I've been put in charge of deciding.

360
25:03.700 --> 25:04.801
You all have one month

361
25:05.301 --> 25:06.680
to prove yourselves

362
25:06.702 --> 25:08.300
and show why you deserve to stay.

363
25:10.542 --> 25:11.543
I'm sorry.

364
25:12.400 --> 25:13.601
I really don't want to do this.

365
25:14.467 --> 25:16.920
But the official order has been issued, so I have to follow it.

366
25:20.760 --> 25:21.761
Toey.

367
25:23.400 --> 25:24.520
I'm one of the two

368
25:25.920 --> 25:26.921
who has to go, right?

369
25:29.307 --> 25:31.320
Just tell me. I can take it.

370
25:32.720 --> 25:36.860
Toey, you know who you need to fire.

371
25:37.955 --> 25:39.464
You mean Mutta, ma'am?

372
25:41.400 --> 25:45.180
It's the only way to put an end to the scandal in our ministry.

373
25:47.500 --> 25:48.801
You care about this ministry, don't you?

374
25:49.501 --> 25:50.502
Yeah.

375
25:58.027 --> 26:00.027
Don't worry, Ta.

376
26:00.176 --> 26:02.177
You can join my insurance sales team.

377
26:02.240 --> 26:04.600
With looks like yours, you'll sell policies like hotcakes.

378
26:06.374 --> 26:09.616
Everyone, let this be a lesson to you.

379
26:10.459 --> 26:14.160
If you want to get ahead, work hard at your desk,

380
26:14.518 --> 26:16.360
not in someone else's bed.

381
26:18.438 --> 26:20.480
I warned you before, you know.

382
26:20.795 --> 26:22.640
But you just kept acting all high and mighty.

383
26:22.912 --> 26:24.080
And look where that got you.

384
26:24.200 --> 26:25.701
Game over!

385
26:26.128 --> 26:30.619
Ta, when are you packing up your things? Just let me know.

386
26:30.752 --> 26:33.000
I've got plenty of cardboard boxes at home.

387
26:33.046 --> 26:34.600
I drink a lot of beer, you see.

388
26:35.247 --> 26:38.480
Have you decided where you want your farewell party?

389
26:39.120 --> 26:43.040
Just let me know. I'll book a place for you.

390
26:48.019 --> 26:49.120
Everyone,

391
26:49.500 --> 26:51.360
please stop rubbing salt in Ta's wounds.

392
26:52.542 --> 26:54.120
She just made a bad choice

393
26:54.467 --> 26:56.168
by having an affair with the Director.

394
26:57.176 --> 26:59.544
Now that she's being fired from the civil service,

395
26:59.587 --> 27:02.480
I'm sure she'll learn her lesson and change her ways.

396
27:03.091 --> 27:05.960
She probably won't dare go after another woman's husband again.

397
27:09.200 --> 27:12.680
Ta, I really don't know what to say, so...

398
27:13.827 --> 27:15.128
I guess I won't say anything.

399
27:20.019 --> 27:24.040
I think you should all worry about yourselves instead.

400
27:24.526 --> 27:27.080
At least I know my fate, so I can relax.

401
27:27.886 --> 27:31.920
I won't have to spend the next month worrying myself sick.

402
27:32.331 --> 27:33.800
It's the rest of you

403
27:34.176 --> 27:37.160
who'll have to fight to impress Toey.

404
27:38.374 --> 27:40.040
I wonder

405
27:42.152 --> 27:44.153
who'll be joining me on the way out.

406
28:05.488 --> 28:07.000
Getting fired is a good thing.

407
28:07.262 --> 28:09.263
Now you can finally work here full-time.

408
28:10.263 --> 28:11.264
See?

409
28:11.300 --> 28:13.601
I've hired more people to help us code the Smart Card system.

410
28:17.158 --> 28:19.359
But that means I'll have fewer chances to see Jenphop.

411
28:20.288 --> 28:23.320
It's much easier to run into him at the Ministry than outside.

412
28:25.289 --> 28:28.382
Oh, have you talked to Veekit yet?

413
28:28.800 --> 28:30.001
Did you find out anything?

414
28:30.179 --> 28:33.240
I did, but I haven't learned anything new.

415
28:33.859 --> 28:35.320
I've only just realized

416
28:35.646 --> 28:37.880
that he has a nasty temper too.

417
28:38.478 --> 28:39.720
Because when I talked to Veekit,

418
28:39.923 --> 28:42.960
he said he'd never helped Jenphop do anything seriously wrong.

419
28:43.816 --> 28:44.817
Who knows?

420
28:45.918 --> 28:48.019
The uncle and nephew might be working together.

421
28:48.300 --> 28:49.301
How can we trust him?

422
28:50.520 --> 28:51.521
True.

423
28:52.700 --> 28:53.920
But I have someone else in mind

424
28:54.601 --> 28:56.800
who can give us inside information on Jenphop.

425
28:58.370 --> 28:59.371
Who?

426
28:59.720 --> 29:00.721
Tetris.

427
29:00.821 --> 29:01.822
Huh?

428
29:02.160 --> 29:04.032
You're going after both of his children?

429
29:04.464 --> 29:07.165
I've talked to Titus. She's still too young.

430
29:07.312 --> 29:08.747
She doesn't know much about what the adults are up to.

431
29:08.971 --> 29:12.572
But Tetris seems to know everything about his parents' problems.

432
29:12.972 --> 29:14.560
How are you going to talk to him?

433
29:14.864 --> 29:17.665
Didn't you say he couldn't stand you?

434
29:18.592 --> 29:22.320
Titus told me her brother likes chatting with guys on an app.

435
29:22.420 --> 29:23.760
His profile picture is a mermaid.

436
29:27.774 --> 29:28.775
Hi.

437
29:37.315 --> 29:38.800
Hi. What's your name?

438
29:39.550 --> 29:40.840
M. You?

439
29:42.099 --> 29:43.100
Wonyoung.

440
29:44.692 --> 29:46.360
Are there mermaids in Korea?

441
29:49.900 --> 29:52.300
Doesn't your boyfriend mind you using this app?

442
29:53.739 --> 29:54.840
Are you asking if I'm single?

443
29:56.200 --> 29:58.880
No, I'm just worried you might already have a boyfriend.

444
29:59.798 --> 30:01.450
I'm single. We can chat.

445
30:02.251 --> 30:03.414
I'm single too.

446
30:04.070 --> 30:06.371
I'm sick of my family. Just looking for someone to talk to.

447
30:06.750 --> 30:08.151
I'm sick of mine too.

448
30:09.083 --> 30:10.084
Who are you sick of?

449
30:10.784 --> 30:13.180
My dad. He's a womanizer.

450
30:13.891 --> 30:15.320
Oh, same here!

451
30:15.571 --> 30:16.620
That's what all straight men are like.

452
30:18.478 --> 30:19.960
Looks like we're in the same boat.

453
30:20.184 --> 30:22.085
Wanna keep chatting?

454
30:23.400 --> 30:25.901
Sure. First one to disappear loses.

455
30:27.100 --> 30:28.101
You're on!

456
30:30.654 --> 30:32.088
I'll get close to Tetris

457
30:32.371 --> 30:33.920
and slowly trick him into revealing information.

458
30:34.400 --> 30:37.360
Kids with troubled families need someone to confide in.

459
30:37.784 --> 30:41.747
He might end up telling a complete stranger everything.

460
30:50.790 --> 30:51.791
Let's go.

461
30:55.171 --> 30:56.172
Goodbye!

462
31:01.070 --> 31:02.071
Tetris.

463
31:03.171 --> 31:04.172
Yes?

464
31:04.747 --> 31:05.840
We're at school.

465
31:07.748 --> 31:09.700
- Bye, Veekit! - Wait, wait!

466
31:09.974 --> 31:12.760
Who are you chatting with? You've been on your phone since breakfast.

467
31:14.395 --> 31:15.396
Your boyfriend?

468
31:16.000 --> 31:17.776
No, just a friend.

469
31:59.518 --> 32:00.600
Yeah, right. Like anyone would believe that.

470
32:00.904 --> 32:03.400
Just bumped into an alpaca at the Ministry.

471
32:04.200 --> 32:05.801
I told you to call me Al Pacino!

472
32:07.251 --> 32:10.734
So who were you chatting with? You weren't even watching where you were going.

473
32:11.616 --> 32:13.760
Well, why didn't you move if you saw me coming?

474
32:14.368 --> 32:16.100
Because I wanted you to bump into me so I could tease you.

475
32:18.283 --> 32:20.640
You and my uncle have one thing in common.

476
32:21.320 --> 32:22.480
You both flirt with every woman you meet.

477
32:23.851 --> 32:25.160
But there's one big difference.

478
32:25.296 --> 32:28.160
If I ever get married, I'd never cheat like my uncle.

479
32:29.531 --> 32:30.720
Is that your pickup line?

480
32:31.300 --> 32:32.301
That's so cringe.

481
32:33.720 --> 32:36.414
Since when is being faithful cringe?

482
32:37.827 --> 32:40.640
Oh, or do you prefer bad boys like my uncle?

483
32:42.107 --> 32:44.800
Aren't you afraid Uncle Phop will come after you for talking to me like this?

484
32:45.510 --> 32:46.511
Not at all.

485
32:47.100 --> 32:48.101
Veekit!

486
32:54.950 --> 32:55.951
Hey!

487
32:57.150 --> 32:59.720
Don't you have anything better to do?

488
33:00.720 --> 33:03.960
If you don't have enough work, I'll find you more.

489
33:05.272 --> 33:08.718
No, sir. I was just saying hi to Ta as a friend.

490
33:09.283 --> 33:12.800
And flirting a little, since I'm single.

491
33:16.731 --> 33:17.880
Talk to you later, Ta.

492
33:21.968 --> 33:22.969
Excuse me.

493
33:29.707 --> 33:30.960
Was he flirting with you?

494
33:31.435 --> 33:32.436
Yes.

495
33:32.624 --> 33:35.760
He has been for a while, and he seems to be getting more serious.

496
33:36.488 --> 33:38.880
Then stop talking to him. I don't like it.

497
33:42.435 --> 33:43.950
And what if I don't?

498
33:45.918 --> 33:48.480
Ta, what's gotten into you lately?

499
33:49.963 --> 33:51.481
You've been provoking me over and over.

500
33:52.283 --> 33:54.160
Why can't you listen to me like you used to?

501
33:55.659 --> 33:57.440
I used to do everything you told me?

502
33:57.864 --> 33:59.300
I never disobeyed you?

503
33:59.427 --> 34:01.224
That's right.

504
34:02.739 --> 34:05.843
You used to be so sweet and obedient.

505
34:10.630 --> 34:13.300
But come to think of it, I like this rebellious side of you too.

506
34:14.875 --> 34:15.876
Hey,

507
34:16.491 --> 34:19.400
when are we finally going to have some wild fun again?

508
34:22.830 --> 34:24.589
I haven't really been in the mood lately.

509
34:25.200 --> 34:28.240
You know I'm getting fired at the end of this month, right?

510
34:28.768 --> 34:30.400
If you can't help me,

511
34:31.014 --> 34:32.440
then you'll just have to take care of yourself.

512
34:33.190 --> 34:34.240
Oh, come on, Ta!

513
34:34.387 --> 34:37.320
I've been taking care of myself so much my hand's practically peeling.

514
34:40.590 --> 34:42.250
I think it's getting rubbed raw.

515
34:51.900 --> 34:52.901
He's here.

516
34:53.648 --> 34:55.500
- Good morning, Toey! - Good morning, Toey!

517
34:55.600 --> 34:58.891
Let me carry that for you. Watch your step.

518
34:58.939 --> 35:00.278
Careful not to trip.

519
35:00.342 --> 35:02.840
Here are the documents you need to sign today.

520
35:02.907 --> 35:05.708
I've organized everything neatly in here for you.

521
35:05.787 --> 35:07.440
Just open it up, and they're ready to sign.

522
35:07.480 --> 35:09.520
This way, please. Watch your step. Careful not to trip.

523
35:12.600 --> 35:13.840
- Hey, old lady! - Huh?

524
35:14.120 --> 35:15.321
Aren't we going to do anything?

525
35:16.200 --> 35:19.120
Look at those bitches!

526
35:19.140 --> 35:21.536
They've already started sucking up to him like crazy.

527
35:22.448 --> 35:23.664
Don't pay them any attention, Sak.

528
35:24.112 --> 35:26.438
We're both valuable employees.

529
35:26.859 --> 35:30.120
We work hard and earn every baht of taxpayers' money.

530
35:30.860 --> 35:32.987
There's no way Toey will fire us.

531
35:34.824 --> 35:35.825
This color is pretty, isn't it?

532
35:35.880 --> 35:37.760
- It really complements my skin tone. - It's gorgeous!

533
35:39.147 --> 35:42.400
Hey, Hong, aren't you going to try to impress him too?

534
35:42.891 --> 35:45.500
You're the youngest here. You might be the first to go.

535
35:47.563 --> 35:51.832
I'm confident I've always worked hard and done my best.

536
35:52.894 --> 35:55.600
I'm sure Toey will recognize my dedication.

537
35:56.419 --> 35:57.840
Don't worry.

538
35:58.752 --> 35:59.796
You're under my wing.

539
36:00.424 --> 36:02.632
I've already told Toey not to fire you.

540
36:05.678 --> 36:07.300
Thank you so much, ma'am.

541
36:18.667 --> 36:20.688
But I feel so sorry for you.

542
36:21.942 --> 36:24.080
Who could be so cruel

543
36:24.406 --> 36:28.840
as to tell you about her affair with the Director?

544
36:29.752 --> 36:34.110
Otherwise, you wouldn't be getting pushed out like this.

545
36:36.000 --> 36:37.592
It must be someone right here in this office.

546
36:37.950 --> 36:40.320
Who knows? It might even be you, Hong.

547
36:41.539 --> 36:42.540
Ta!

548
36:44.200 --> 36:45.960
Why would you say that?

549
36:47.294 --> 36:50.720
You know how much I adore you.

550
36:53.100 --> 36:54.101
I'm just kidding.

551
36:56.195 --> 36:57.196
Ta!

552
37:23.558 --> 37:26.720
I got up early this morning to prepare all the documents.

553
37:27.243 --> 37:30.440
- This way, Toey! - Whisky, open the door!

554
37:30.616 --> 37:32.640
- After you, Toey! - Please, Toey!

555
37:33.480 --> 37:36.070
- Welcome, Toey! - Welcome, Toey!

556
37:36.088 --> 37:37.464
Your coffee, Toey.

557
37:37.502 --> 37:39.000
And your salad.

558
37:40.901 --> 37:41.902
Hey!

559
37:43.317 --> 37:45.200
Instead of wasting time sucking up to him,

560
37:45.680 --> 37:49.520
why don't you focus on doing some actual work and proving your worth?

561
37:51.267 --> 37:53.043
Go on! Get back to work!

562
37:54.979 --> 37:57.920
Or I'll report you to Mrs. Nopnapha.

563
38:00.878 --> 38:02.200
Ugh, the coffee will just have to go.

564
38:04.486 --> 38:05.487
Toey.

565
38:06.544 --> 38:09.675
I'm not the other person getting fired, am I?

566
38:10.182 --> 38:11.608
I can't tell you that yet.

567
38:12.183 --> 38:13.190
I'm still evaluating everyone.

568
38:13.626 --> 38:14.925
I'll make my decision at the end of the month.

569
38:15.576 --> 38:17.920
But I'm next in line to take over your position.

570
38:19.086 --> 38:21.720
If you fire me, who's going to succeed you?

571
38:22.126 --> 38:23.127
Sak, of course.

572
38:23.646 --> 38:25.667
He's been here almost as long as you have.

573
38:25.971 --> 38:27.520
And his performance is just as good as yours.

574
38:28.446 --> 38:31.280
That King Kong-sized queen? As good as me?

575
38:32.878 --> 38:35.320
When it comes to document formatting and page margins,

576
38:35.688 --> 38:39.480
I guarantee no one in this entire ministry is as meticulous as me!

577
38:40.678 --> 38:43.440
But Sak is also really good at making perfectly neat pleats in tablecloths.

578
38:52.395 --> 38:54.155
Phorn, what are you doing?

579
39:02.582 --> 39:03.583
Toey.

580
39:07.531 --> 39:10.920
I'm showing you another one of my special talents.

581
39:11.840 --> 39:13.320
Just for you, Toey.

582
39:19.200 --> 39:20.201
Toey.

583
39:24.000 --> 39:26.001
Has the pickled shellfish you ordered from your mom arrived yet?

584
39:26.123 --> 39:27.480
It should arrive tomorrow.

585
39:28.500 --> 39:30.101
So what are you selling these days?

586
39:32.547 --> 39:34.080
Ta.

587
39:35.038 --> 39:36.840
Since you're leaving at the end of the month,

588
39:37.379 --> 39:39.550
you might as well do some work before you go.

589
39:40.430 --> 39:41.431
Here.

590
39:42.552 --> 39:45.560
Once you're done, put it on my desk.

591
39:47.715 --> 39:51.000
Uncle Somsak, do you know what report I'm drafting?

592
39:52.323 --> 39:54.680
No. How would I know?

593
39:54.878 --> 39:56.723
Your work isn't my responsibility.

594
39:57.315 --> 40:00.080
It's a report on all the pointless things our department does.

595
40:00.520 --> 40:04.040
Every day, we convert paper documents into digital files,

596
40:04.539 --> 40:06.480
then print those digital files back onto paper.

597
40:06.971 --> 40:09.880
The content stays the same. Only the date changes.

598
40:10.094 --> 40:11.920
Then we run around getting signatures from everyone in the Ministry,

599
40:12.350 --> 40:13.520
before filing everything away again.

600
40:14.798 --> 40:16.520
I'm sending this report straight to the Prime Minister.

601
40:16.995 --> 40:18.800
Maybe it'll finally bring about some changes.

602
40:21.192 --> 40:24.824
Sure. Good luck with your little revolution!

603
40:25.310 --> 40:28.403
Millions of people have probably had the same idea.

604
40:28.734 --> 40:30.320
But this is the civil service.

605
40:30.500 --> 40:33.840
We've been doing things this way since you were still a sperm cell.

606
40:34.051 --> 40:37.704
And we'll keep doing it until the end of the world.

607
40:41.520 --> 40:45.600
Listen here, Mutta.

608
40:45.768 --> 40:50.440
You're already in the final days of your civil service career.

609
40:50.966 --> 40:52.320
Just get on with it.

610
40:52.367 --> 40:56.022
Type away, take it easy, and do the bare minimum.

611
40:56.200 --> 40:59.500
Before you know it, it'll be 2 p.m. Time to put on your makeup and go home.

612
40:59.600 --> 41:02.040
Why make life so complicated, right?

613
41:02.448 --> 41:03.449
Exactly.

614
41:04.118 --> 41:08.360
Mutta, you're lucky you actually have work to do.

615
41:08.752 --> 41:10.840
Look at the two of us.

616
41:11.400 --> 41:15.560
We've been filing our nails so much our fingers are about to fall off.

617
41:20.758 --> 41:22.920
Thank you, Cha-am, for pointing out the problem.

618
41:23.083 --> 41:26.700
Now I can include overstaffing in my report too.

619
41:27.526 --> 41:30.840
Actually, laying off just two people probably isn't enough.

620
41:31.216 --> 41:34.840
They should get rid of half the staff to stop wasting taxpayers' money.

621
41:36.900 --> 41:38.901
Who's got nothing to do?

622
41:39.100 --> 41:41.120
Look! I'm reusing paper!

623
41:41.648 --> 41:42.649
See?

624
41:42.939 --> 41:44.500
Cha-am, get over here and help me!

625
41:45.451 --> 41:48.600
And I am busy making photocopies too.

626
41:50.824 --> 41:53.966
Ta, I'll take care of these documents for you.

627
41:54.440 --> 41:56.200
I'm trying to prove how hardworking I am.

628
41:59.832 --> 42:02.920
Hong, would you like to take some of this work?

629
42:03.347 --> 42:06.942
No, thanks. I've always been dedicated to my work.

630
42:07.336 --> 42:10.414
I'm sure the Ministry will recognize my hard work.

631
42:11.337 --> 42:12.338
Fine, I'll do it myself.

632
42:26.606 --> 42:29.515
Hey, have you ever stumbled upon any of your dad's secrets?

633
42:31.323 --> 42:34.520
You mean his mistress? Dad never tried to hide that.

634
42:34.790 --> 42:36.191
So I wouldn't really call it a secret.

635
42:46.230 --> 42:49.040
What about secrets between your dad and his mistress?

636
42:50.134 --> 42:51.200
I have no idea.

637
42:51.435 --> 42:53.200
That homewrecking bitch works for my dad.

638
42:53.360 --> 42:56.300
If they have any secrets, they're probably hidden at work.

639
42:56.715 --> 42:59.520
You mean in your dad's office?

640
43:00.358 --> 43:02.400
Yeah. I've never snooped around in there.

641
43:02.814 --> 43:04.500
Why do you ask? You sound like a detective.

642
43:04.776 --> 43:07.438
Oh, I'm investigating my dad's mistress.

643
43:07.656 --> 43:09.960
I want to know where adults hide their secrets.

644
43:17.875 --> 43:19.040
What's that noise?

645
43:24.027 --> 43:25.963
Hey! What's that noise?

646
43:28.992 --> 43:30.440
Is there a fire, everyone?

647
43:31.400 --> 43:32.601
Let's get out of here!

648
43:32.620 --> 43:35.200
Hey, it's just another fire drill. No need to run.

649
43:35.486 --> 43:38.160
But we didn't get any notice about a fire drill.

650
43:38.238 --> 43:40.440
Fire! Fire!

651
43:42.339 --> 43:43.640
The fire escape is this way, Uncle!

652
43:46.038 --> 43:48.640
Everyone, the other departments are already evacuating!

653
43:48.800 --> 43:50.001
Then let's get moving!

654
43:52.520 --> 43:54.520
But I haven't finished making photocopies!

655
43:55.515 --> 43:57.240
Then take them with you, you idiot!

656
44:11.600 --> 44:13.180
Fine, I'll just leave them!

657
44:43.400 --> 44:45.401
[Browsing History: Assassin]

658
44:45.501 --> 44:46.502
[No results found]

659
44:49.920 --> 44:51.921
[Contract Killing: 1 result found]

660
45:16.696 --> 45:19.320
Who the hell put us on the 21st floor?

661
45:19.672 --> 45:21.520
Why couldn't they put us on the third?

662
45:21.621 --> 45:23.459
Hey, you lot!

663
45:24.264 --> 45:25.598
Why didn't any of you wait for me?

664
45:25.650 --> 45:27.880
Where the hell have you been, old lady?

665
45:27.900 --> 45:29.651
And look at you! Why are you such a mess?

666
45:30.179 --> 45:32.126
Hey, are you staring at my boobs?

667
45:32.595 --> 45:33.320
How disgusting!

668
45:33.566 --> 45:35.320
I was running down the fire escape.

669
45:35.344 --> 45:38.000
Things just started falling off with every exhausting flight of stairs.

670
45:38.163 --> 45:42.540
So, does everyone see the importance of fire insurance now?

671
45:42.894 --> 45:44.320
Let's sign up right now.

672
45:44.387 --> 45:47.262
I'm determined to sell at least eight policies today.

673
45:47.448 --> 45:49.049
You're still trying to sell insurance?

674
45:49.320 --> 45:50.920
Is everyone okay?

675
45:52.475 --> 45:55.400
Veekit, I ran all the way down.

676
45:55.579 --> 45:57.280
My legs are completely weak.

677
45:57.936 --> 45:59.670
Where's Ta? Where is she?

678
46:00.016 --> 46:01.080
Has anyone seen Ta?

679
46:01.411 --> 46:06.000
Oh, I saw her leave the office a while before the alarm went off.

680
46:06.142 --> 46:09.040
Maybe she's already downstairs with another group.

681
46:09.760 --> 46:12.920
You seem awfully worried about Ta, Veekit.

682
46:13.038 --> 46:15.240
Almost like you're husband and wife.

683
46:15.260 --> 46:17.261
Hey! Slap yourself across the mouth right now.

684
46:17.400 --> 46:20.520
How could she be the nephew's wife when she's already the uncle's mistress? Disgusting!

685
46:21.278 --> 46:23.584
Wait, is everyone here?

686
46:23.700 --> 46:24.701
Oh, right!

687
46:25.147 --> 46:28.870
Apart from Ta, is anyone else missing?

688
46:29.920 --> 46:32.560
Toey! Toey must still be upstairs!

689
46:34.272 --> 46:35.820
The photocopier!

690
46:38.438 --> 46:39.439
Ta!

691
46:40.763 --> 46:43.000
Toey must have fainted upstairs.

692
46:43.064 --> 46:45.360
I'll go rescue him myself.

693
46:45.502 --> 46:48.110
Stop right there! You're just going up to rescue Toey to score points with him!

694
46:48.200 --> 46:50.801
You think someone in your condition can carry Toey downstairs?

695
46:50.894 --> 46:53.726
No way! You're old as hell, you hag!

696
46:53.811 --> 46:55.440
Hey, stop it! Don't underestimate me!

697
46:55.452 --> 46:57.400
I do aerobics at Lumpini Park every day!

698
46:57.453 --> 47:00.200
You? How strong can you possibly be? Let's see what you've got!

699
47:00.220 --> 47:01.640
There! I thought you did aerobics at Lumpini Park!

700
47:01.660 --> 47:04.360
- You wanna fight, you bitch? - Come on, then! Show me how strong you are!

701
47:04.395 --> 47:06.320
Come at me! Come on, you old hag!

702
47:06.560 --> 47:08.561
- Come on, you old hag! Bring it! - Uncle Sak!

703
47:08.600 --> 47:09.601
Auntie Phorn!

704
47:09.686 --> 47:10.687
- What? - What?

705
47:11.824 --> 47:13.440
Everyone's already gone.

706
47:13.518 --> 47:14.519
Huh?

707
47:14.792 --> 47:16.360
- Toey! - Toey!

708
47:17.280 --> 47:18.480
Toey!

709
47:19.368 --> 47:23.550
Oh, why did those idiots even run back upstairs?

710
48:10.896 --> 48:12.880
Oh my God, Toey!

711
48:13.097 --> 48:14.680
Are you okay, Toey?

712
48:14.696 --> 48:15.697
Come on.

713
48:16.400 --> 48:17.401
Let me help you.

714
48:18.467 --> 48:20.250
Wait, wait. I'm not that bad.

715
48:20.728 --> 48:23.160
My blood sugar's low, my blood pressure's high,

716
48:23.230 --> 48:26.060
my asthma's acting up, and I'm having a panic attack.

717
48:26.131 --> 48:28.560
Okay, then. Let me help you. Come on.

718
48:28.718 --> 48:30.400
Get over here, you idiots! Hurry!

719
48:32.398 --> 48:33.560
Toey, are you okay?

720
48:35.347 --> 48:36.880
- Can you manage? - One, two, three!

721
48:37.870 --> 48:40.200
- I'm scared! - One, two, three!

722
48:42.190 --> 48:43.347
That's enough! Stop!

723
48:44.413 --> 48:46.040
You idiots are no help at all!

724
48:46.158 --> 48:47.800
Come here! Move aside! I'll do it myself!

725
48:48.760 --> 48:49.761
Get out of the way, you old hag!

726
48:50.568 --> 48:53.600
Toey! Toey! Come on!

727
48:53.710 --> 48:55.720
Let me help you, Toey.

728
48:56.000 --> 48:57.001
Thank you so much, Sak.

729
49:00.310 --> 49:01.320
I'll go ahead, then.

730
49:09.923 --> 49:11.520
Who the hell slashed my tires?

731
49:11.608 --> 49:14.309
Meow! She deliberately sabotaged you!

732
49:14.533 --> 49:15.534
Meow!

733
49:15.942 --> 49:18.800
You lying old hag! You're the one who stabbed Uncle Sak in the back!

734
49:18.843 --> 49:22.080
Uncle? Who are you calling Uncle? You deserve a slap!

735
49:24.342 --> 49:27.400
Toey, since you're about to be burned alive anyway,

736
49:27.622 --> 49:28.886
please just tell us

737
49:29.147 --> 49:31.720
who the other person getting fired is!

738
49:34.982 --> 49:36.400
Stop! Stop right there!

739
49:36.598 --> 49:38.280
I'm not telling anyone who it is

740
49:38.662 --> 49:41.560
- until you all help me first! - Chuenchom!

741
49:41.744 --> 49:43.493
Go find something to wheel Toey out on!

742
49:45.230 --> 49:46.231
Everyone!

743
49:46.632 --> 49:48.320
What the hell do you need that for?

744
50:03.486 --> 50:04.887
Wait, wait!

745
50:08.462 --> 50:11.480
Now I realize just how much you all love me.

746
50:13.304 --> 50:14.880
I'll resign myself

747
50:16.160 --> 50:17.861
so everyone else can keep their jobs.

748
50:24.288 --> 50:27.560
Everyone! The fire escape is this way!

749
50:35.384 --> 50:37.400
Toey!

750
51:24.155 --> 51:25.156
Ta.

751
51:25.371 --> 51:26.372
Veekit.

752
51:33.864 --> 51:34.865
What are you doing in here?

753
51:39.440 --> 51:40.441
[Hong]

754
51:47.056 --> 51:48.960
You've known about the Director and Hong all along, haven't you?

755
52:08.854 --> 52:09.855
Hong!

756
52:10.816 --> 52:11.817
Wait!

757
52:12.779 --> 52:14.500
I know everything about you and the Director.

758
52:14.667 --> 52:17.560
Ta, you can't tell anyone about this!

759
52:17.696 --> 52:19.643
I'm begging you, Ta!

760
52:19.915 --> 52:22.120
From now on, you'll have to help me with my work

761
52:22.539 --> 52:23.920
whenever I need you.

762
52:25.606 --> 52:26.779
She's pregnant.

763
52:27.083 --> 52:30.160
- How the hell is that possible? - Because you slept with her!

764
52:30.696 --> 52:31.840
Ta, are you really pregnant?

765
52:32.280 --> 52:33.281
Yes.

766
52:33.694 --> 52:35.320
But I'm not having an abortion.

767
52:36.323 --> 52:37.560
I'm keeping the baby.

768
52:41.827 --> 52:43.600
- No, no! - Get her!
